        "original_id": "e18d0f90-47f2-5b2e-bc22-c27b0aa4d986",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Smith\n- Bands: Supergrass, Quietdrive, PJ Harvey, Elastica, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, The Scissor Sisters, Arcade Fire, Arctic Monkeys, Blur\n- Companies: EMI Publishing\n- Places: Oxford, Hopkins, Minnesota\n- Topics: band formations, A&R signings\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Mike Smith moved to EMI Publishing.\n- At EMI Publishing, Mike Smith signed acts including PJ Harvey, Elastica, Supergrass, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, The Scissor Sisters, Arcade Fire, and Arctic Monkeys.\n- At EMI Publishing, Mike Smith re-signed Blur and progressed to the position of Head of A&R.\n- In 1993, Supergrass formed in Oxford as an English rock band.\n- In 2002, Quietdrive formed as an alternative rock band based in Hopkins, Minnesota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
